# UI Design Consistency Rules

- Keep all first-party pages in a unified dark minimalist style.
- Use color tokens consistently:
  - background `#000000`
  - panel `#111111`
  - border `#222222`
  - primary text `#ffffff`
  - secondary text `#666666`
- Reuse action button styling across pages:
  - uppercase labels
  - solid 1px border
  - hover by border emphasis (not heavy shadows)
- Keep layout language consistent with the ticket board:
  - bold title + subtle subtitle
  - header with bottom border
  - card/table surfaces with thin borders
- Avoid gradient backgrounds and rounded glossy components unless explicitly requested.
- Do not use browser-native modal dialogs (`prompt`, `alert`, `confirm`) for first-party UI flows. Collect input and show feedback with in-page components (dropdown panels, inline forms, or custom modal surfaces that follow project styles).
- When adding new pages, include navigation entry points from main board and stats when relevant.
